    "sections": [],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I check a marketing agency name is free?",
        "answer": "Press Check on any name to see whether it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. In the UK, search Companies House; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Check your local area too, as two similar names nearby confuse customers."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I name a marketing agency?",
        "answer": "Agencies usually pick one of three shapes: the founders' surnames (\"Hartley & Rowe\"), which sounds established; a short brandable name (\"Magpie Studio\", \"Fox & Feather\"), which shows creative flair; or a clever line about what you do (\"Stop the Scroll Social\"). Say \"Digital\", \"Social\" or \"Creative\" if you specialise, and make sure the name works as a handle, because clients will look you up on social media first."
      }
    ]
